  "Number": 20,
  "Question": "What is the measure of the acute angle formed by the hands of a clock at \\(4{:}20\\) a.m.?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(0^{\\circ}\\)",
    "B": "\\(5^{\\circ}\\)",
    "C": "\\(8^{\\circ}\\)",
    "D": "\\(10^{\\circ}\\)",
    "E": "\\(12^{\\circ}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "At \\(4{:}20\\), the minute hand points exactly to the \\(4\\). The hour hand has already moved partway from \\(4\\) toward \\(5\\).\n\nThe \\(12\\) hour marks divide a full turn equally, so neighboring marks are\n\\[\n360^\\circ\\div12=30^\\circ\n\\]\napart. The hour hand takes \\(60\\) minutes to move through this gap. In \\(20\\) minutes it moves one-third of the gap, or\n\\[\n\\frac{20}{60}\\cdot30^\\circ=10^\\circ.\n\\]\nThus the hands are \\(\\boxed{10^\\circ}\\) apart. This angle is acute, so the answer is choice \\(\\text{D}\\).",
